>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `add_split`

``` hol4
simpLib.add_split : thm -> simpset -> simpset
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Adds a split rule to a simpset.

`add_split th ss` adds a looper applying `splitLib.SPLIT_TAC [th]`. The
looper is named `split name`, or `split_asm name` for an assumption
rule, where `name` is the database name of `th`, or `thy$c` if `th` is
unnamed and its redex has head constant `thy$c`. Adding a rule with the
same looper name replaces the old one. `ExclX "split:name"` disables the
rule for one call; see [`simpLib.ExclX`](#simpLib.ExclX).

### Failure

Fails if `th` is not a split rule.

### Example

``` hol4
>> val c = Context.snapshot();
>>_ val opt_ss = simpLib.add_split (splitLib.type_split_of “:'a option”)
                   bool_ss;
>> SIMP_TAC opt_ss []
     ([], “P (case x of NONE => 0 | SOME n => n + 1) : bool”) c;
>> SIMP_TAC opt_ss [ExclX "split:option$option_CASE"]
     ([], “P (case x of NONE => 0 | SOME n => n + 1) : bool”) c;
```

